      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. it's okay, i guess. the structure is a bit... much. it feels a little disjointed with all those extra bullet points at the end that don't really add much technical value. \n\nthe linter score for this draft was decent, but it's still a bit low for the \"comprehensive\" tier we're aiming for in the official docs. can you try to expand on the guide a bit more? try to add more detail to each step so it's a more substantial guide, and feel free to use more headers or lists to make the individual components of the process stand out more clearly. just make sure it's still technically accurate.",
      "source": "evaluator"
